    fix: suppress unclassified row on confident match output. Addresses LORE-046.
    
    Real-use dogfood hit: 'python -m lore match "drain 503"' printed a second
    'unclassified confidence=0.00 evidence: none' line under every confident
    match — output read like two answers and line-splitting consumers saw two
    class rows.
    
    Display-level only (lore/classifier.py untouched): _cmd_match filters the
    unclassified fallback from the PRINTED candidates when --explain is unset;
    a true miss (fallback = only candidate) still prints it honestly, the
    empty-list 'no candidates' exit-1 branch is unchanged, and --explain keeps
    the raw list (fallback row + near-misses) for evidence transparency.
    
    Docs sync: verbatim match examples in README.md and docs/INSTALL.md no
    longer show the fallback row (true-miss and --explain examples keep it,
    verified against live output). Count sync: scripts/test-count.txt and the
    README/CONTRIBUTING/INSTALL literals now 415 (was 404; +11 LORE-046 tests).
    
    Verified: pytest 415 passed; ruff check + format --check clean;
    check-test-count.sh PASS (class-count=13 derived); live match checks.
